  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Request lifecycle (order is load-bearing)",
      "items": [
        "Guards run before interceptors: 429/401/403 never reach MetricsInterceptor; an Express response middleware counts them instead.",
        "1 TieredThrottlerGuard \u2192 2 ClsGuard \u2192 3 UnifiedAuthGuard \u2192 4 TenantLockGuard \u2192 5 PatientConsentGuard \u2192 6 TenantOwnedResourceSSEGuard \u2192 7 OriginTenantBindingGuard \u2192 8 RequiresIfMatchGuard.",
        "Interceptors: Metrics \u2192 RateLimitHeaders \u2192 Context \u2192 Exception \u2192 Maintenance \u2192 ImpersonationAudit \u2192 ETag (ETag is registered from main.ts).",
        "Filters: AllExceptions \u2192 HttpExceptionEnvelope \u2192 DataNotFound \u2192 Consent; Nest consults the LAST registered matching filter first."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Identity, authz and tenancy",
      "items": [
        "UnifiedAuthGuard is deny-by-default and accepts JWT, API key, service account and stream tickets; unknown credential classes fail closed.",
        "AuthorizationGuard applies CASL/RBAC abilities at controller/route level; PatientConsentGuard adds patient-scoped consent/ABAC.",
        "Tenant isolation: CLS store \u2192 TenantContextProvider/Prisma tenant scope; OriginTenantBindingGuard binds origins; the SSE guard checks resource ownership.",
        "Errors are shaped as 404-over-403 where existence must not leak."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Feature modules (common + feature arrays)",
      "items": [
        "AppModule composes 40 common + 74 feature module entries; the inventory counts 77 module files. Clinical: consultation, history, consent, templates, fact-ledger.",
        "Agent/workflows: agent, agent-admin, agent-promotion, agent-trajectory, workflows (definition/run/sandbox/assignment/node/fixture/invariant), harness-admin, prompt management, MCP admin.",
        "AI platform: ai-inference, ai-model, ai-provider-connection, ai-routing-policy, ai-service-admin, guardrail-*, inference-engines, model-residency, nlp-task-instructions.",
        "Tenancy/storage/ops: tenant, user, rbac, api-key, service-account, auth, entitlements, billing; storage/media; health, audit, webhooks, notifications."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Data, workers and side processes",
      "items": [
        "Prisma is tenant-scoped through TenantContextProvider; Postgres is the transactional store; Redis backs throttling, tickets and BullMQ.",
        "BullMQ jobs cover consultation summaries/entities, DNA reports, RAG ingest, webhook delivery, AI usage outbox, fact ledger, checkpoints and model download.",
        "The checkpoint worker is a separate process for tenant export/restore; the API process keeps only producers.",
        "S3/MinIO stores tenant media and model artifacts; Vault supplies secrets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Boot audits (startup fails closed)",
      "items": [
        "main.ts audits admin route permissions, API-key scopes, internal-route exclusion, admin scope declarations, business-plane exemptions and API-key surface coverage.",
        "It also audits consent route coverage, service-account surface, WebSocket gateway owner binding, CASL enforce-pair reachability and OCC coverage.",
        "OCC coverage is warn-only; the others refuse startup so drift is caught before traffic.",
        "assertJwtSecretNotPlaceholder and GenAI content-capture checks also gate boot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Where the evidence lives",
      "items": [
        "Bootstrap: apps/api/src/main.ts",
        "Global wiring: apps/api/src/app.module.ts",
        "Auth: packages/applications/src/authorization/unified-auth.guard.ts and authorization.guard.ts",
        "Guards: apps/api/src/guards/ and apps/api/src/common/tenant-owned-resource-sse.guard.ts",
        "Filters/interceptors: apps/api/src/filters/ and apps/api/src/interceptors/"
      ]
    }
  ]
}